{"id":"mahabharata-12-016","work":"mahabharata","part":12,"partName":"शान्तिपर्व","partNameEn":"Shanti Parva","unit":16,"title":"षोडशोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 16 · Bhima on the sorrow of the mind","summary":{"en":"Bhima tells his brother that illness of the mind is as real as that of the body, and that the man who keeps to dharma may rule without sorrow. He says the exile and the shame of the dice are not borne by a man who gives up the throne.","kn":"ಮನಸ್ಸಿನ ರೋಗ ದೇಹದ ರೋಗದಂತೆಯೇ ನಿಜ, ಧರ್ಮದಲ್ಲಿ ನಿಂತವನು ದುಃಖವಿಲ್ಲದೆ ಆಳಬಹುದೆಂದು ಭೀಮ ಅಣ್ಣನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ. ಸಿಂಹಾಸನ ತೊರೆದವನು ವನವಾಸ, ಜೂಜಿನ ಅವಮಾನ ಸಹಿಸುವುದಿಲ್ಲವೆನ್ನುತ್ತಾನೆ.","hi":"भीम भाई से कहते हैं कि मन का रोग शरीर के रोग जितना ही सच्चा है, और धर्म में स्थित रहने वाला शोक के बिना राज कर सकता है। वे कहते हैं कि सिंहासन छोड़ने वाला वनवास और द्यूत के अपमान को नहीं सहता।","te":"మనసు రోగం శరీర రోగమంత నిజమని, ధర్మంలో నిలిచినవాడు దుఃఖం లేకుండా పాలించగలడని భీముడు అన్నకు చెబుతాడు. సింహాసనం వదిలినవాడు వనవాసం, జూదం అవమానాన్ని భరించడన్నాడు.","ta":"மனநோய் உடல்நோய் போலவே உண்மையானது, தர்மத்தில் நிற்பவன் துயரின்றி ஆளலாம் என்று பீமன் அண்ணனிடம் கூறுகிறான். அரியணையை விடுபவன் வனவாசம், சூதின் அவமானத்தைத் தாங்கமாட்டான் என்கிறான்.","ml":"മനസ്സിന്റെ രോഗം ശരീരത്തിന്റെ രോഗംപോലെ യാഥാർത്ഥ്യമാണെന്ന് ഭീമൻ സഹോദരനോട് പറയുന്നു; ധർമ്മം പാലിക്കുന്നവന് ദുഃഖമില്ലാതെ ഭരിക്കാമെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു. സിംഹാസനം ഉപേക്ഷിക്കുന്ന മനുഷ്യന് വനവാസവും ചൂതിലെ അപമാനവും സഹിക്കേണ്ടിവരുന്നില്ലെന്ന് അദ്ദേഹം പറയുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 12.16; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Wed Jun 16 2021","sections":[{"title":"राजधर्मपर्व","titleEn":"Rajadharma Parva (Duties of kings)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"अर्जुनस्य वचः श्रुत्वा भीमसेनोऽत्यमर्षणः ।\nधैर्यमास्थाय तेजस्वी ज्येष्ठं भ्रातरमब्रवीत् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Hearing Arjuna's words, the radiant Bhimasena, very impatient, steadied himself and spoke to his eldest brother."}},{"n":2,"text":"राजन्विदितधर्मोऽसि न तेऽस्त्यविदितं भुवि ।\nउपशिक्षाम ते वृत्तं सदैव न च शक्नुमः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima said: King, you know dharma; nothing on earth is unknown to you. We have always learned from your conduct, and yet we cannot match it."}},{"n":3,"text":"न वक्ष्यामि न वक्ष्यामीत्येवं मे मनसि स्थितम् ।\nअतिदुःखात्तु वक्ष्यामि तन्निबोध जनाधिप ॥","meaning":{"en":"I thought, \"I will not speak, I will not speak,\" but out of great pain I shall speak. Listen, lord of the people."}},{"n":4,"text":"भवतस्तु प्रमोहेन सर्वं संशयितं कृतम् ।\nविक्लवत्वं च नः प्राप्तमबलत्वं तथैव च ॥","meaning":{"en":"By your bewilderment everything has been put in doubt, and we have fallen into distraction and weakness."}},{"n":5,"text":"कथं हि राजा लोकस्य सर्वशास्त्रविशारदः ।\nमोहमापद्यते दैन्याद्यथा कुपुरुषस्तथा ॥","meaning":{"en":"How can a king of the world, skilled in all the sciences, fall into confusion through despondency, like a petty man?"}},{"n":6,"text":"आगतिश्च गतिश्चैव लोकस्य विदिता तव ।\nआयत्यां च तदात्वे च न तेऽस्त्यविदितं प्रभो ॥","meaning":{"en":"You know the coming and going of the world, and its future and its present. Nothing is unknown to you, lord."}},{"n":7,"text":"एवं गते महाराज राज्यं प्रति जनाधिप ।\nहेतुमत्र प्रवक्ष्यामि तदिहैकमनाः शृणु ॥","meaning":{"en":"Since matters stand so, great king, concerning the kingdom, I will tell you the reason. Listen here with a single mind."}},{"n":8,"text":"द्विविधो जायते व्याधिः शारीरो मानसस्तथा ।\nपरस्परं तयोर्जन्म निर्द्वंद्वं नोपलभ्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Illness is of two kinds, bodily and mental. Each is born from the other, and neither is found without the other."}},{"n":9,"text":"शारीराज्जायते व्याधिर्मानसो नात्र संशयः ।\nमानसाज्जायते व्याधिः शारीर इति निश्चयः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Mental illness arises from bodily illness, without doubt, and bodily illness arises from mental illness; that is certain."}},{"n":10,"text":"शारीरमानसे दुःखे योऽतीते अनुशोचति ।\nदुःखेन लभते दुःखं द्वावनर्थौ प्रपद्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"He who mourns past bodily and mental pain gets pain from pain and falls into two misfortunes."}},{"n":11,"text":"शीतोष्णे चैव वायुश्च त्रयः शारीरजा गुणाः ।\nतेषां गुणानां साम्यं च तदाहुः स्वस्थलक्षणम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Cold, heat and wind are the three bodily qualities, and their balance is called the sign of health."}},{"n":12,"text":"तेषामन्यतमोत्सेके विधानमुपदिष्यते ।\nउष्णेन बाध्यते शीतं शीतेनोष्णं प्रबाध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"When any one of them rises too much, a remedy is prescribed: heat is overcome by cold, and cold by heat."}},{"n":13,"text":"सत्त्वं रजस्तमश्चैव मानसाः स्युस्त्रयो गुणाः ।\nहर्षेण बाध्यते शोको हर्षः शोकेन बाध्यते ॥","meaning":{"en":"Goodness, passion and darkness are the three qualities of the mind. Grief is overcome by joy, and joy by grief."}},{"n":14,"text":"कश्चित्सुखे वर्तमानो दुःखस्य स्मर्तुमिच्छति ।\nकश्चिद्दुःखे वर्तमानः सुखस्य स्मर्तुमिच्छति ॥","meaning":{"en":"Some who are in happiness want to recall their sorrow, and some who are in sorrow want to recall their happiness."}},{"n":15,"text":"स त्वं न दुःखी दुःखस्य न सुखी च सुखस्य च ।\nन दुःखी सुखजातस्य न सुखी दुःखजस्य वा ॥","meaning":{"en":"Yet you are neither the one in sorrow for sorrow, nor the happy one for happiness; not the sorrowing for what arises from happiness, nor the happy for what arises from sorrow."}},{"n":16,"text":"स्मर्तुमर्हसि कौरव्य दिष्टं तु बलवत्तरम् ।\nअथ वा ते स्वभावोऽयं येन पार्थिव कृष्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"Remember, Kaurava, that fate is stronger still. Or is this simply your own nature, by which you are dragged along, king?"}},{"n":17,"text":"दृष्ट्वा सभागतां कृष्णामेकवस्त्रां रजस्वलाम् ।\nमिषतां पाण्डुपुत्राणां न तस्य स्मर्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You should not recall that you saw Krishna in the assembly, in her season, in a single cloth, as the sons of Pandu looked on."}},{"n":18,"text":"प्रव्राजनं च नगरादजिनैश्च निवासनम् ।\nमहारण्यनिवासश्च न तस्य स्मर्तुमर्हसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"You should not recall the banishment from the city, the living in deerskins, and the dwelling in the great forest."}},{"n":19,"text":"जटासुरात्परिक्लेशं चित्रसेनेन चाहवम् ।\nसैन्धवाच्च परिक्लेशं कथं विस्मृतवानसि ।\nपुनरज्ञातचर्यायां कीचकेन पदा वधम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"How have you forgotten the torment by Jatasura, the fight with Chitrasena, the torment from the Saindhava, and again, in the year of hiding, Kichaka's blow with his foot?"}},{"n":20,"text":"यच्च ते द्रोणभीष्माभ्यां युद्धमासीदरिंदम ।\nमनसैकेन ते युद्धमिदं घोरमुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"The battle you had with Drona and Bhishma, tormentor of foes, has now become a dreadful battle with your mind alone."}},{"n":21,"text":"यत्र नास्ति शरैः कार्यं न मित्रैर्न च बन्धुभिः ।\nआत्मनैकेन योद्धव्यं तत्ते युद्धमुपस्थितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"In it arrows have no use, nor friends, nor kinsmen. It must be fought by oneself alone, and that is the battle that now stands before you."}},{"n":22,"text":"तस्मिन्ननिर्जिते युद्धे प्राणान्यदि ह मोक्ष्यसे ।\nअन्यं देहं समास्थाय पुनस्तेनैव योत्स्यसे ॥","meaning":{"en":"If you give up your breath without winning that battle, you will take another body and fight the same war again."}},{"n":23,"text":"तस्मादद्यैव गन्तव्यं युद्धस्य भरतर्षभ ।\nएतज्जित्वा महाराज कृतकृत्यो भविष्यसि ॥","meaning":{"en":"Therefore, best of the Bharatas, go out to that battle this very day. Winning it, great king, you will have done your task."}},{"n":24,"text":"एतां बुद्धिं विनिश्चित्य भूतानामागतिं गतिम् ।\nपितृपैतामहे वृत्ते शाधि राज्यं यथोचितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Having made this resolve, knowing the coming and going of beings, rule the kingdom as is fitting, following the conduct of your father and grandfather."}},{"n":25,"text":"दिष्ट्या दुर्योधनः पापो निहतः सानुगो युधि ।\nद्रौपद्याः केशपक्षस्य दिष्ट्या त्वं पदवीं गतः ॥","meaning":{"en":"By good fortune the wicked Duryodhana was killed in battle with his followers, and by good fortune you have walked the path of Draupadi's hair."}},{"n":26,"text":"यजस्व वाजिमेधेन विधिवद्दक्षिणावता ।\nवयं ते किंकराः पार्थ वासुदेवश्च वीर्यवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Sacrifice with the horse sacrifice, with its fees, as the rule requires. We are your servants, Partha, and so is mighty Vasudeva."}}]}]}